{:class "event_title"} "Épée, Individual, Men" [:small {}]] [:table {:class "biodata"} [:tbody {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Date"] [:td {} "20 July 1996"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/725"} "Georgia World Congress Center, Atlanta, Georgia"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/114689"} "45 from 21 countries"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Format"] [:td {:colspan "2"} "Single-elimination tournament."]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "According to the seeding, " [:a {:href "/athletes/23274"} "Aleksandr Beketov"] " was expected to exit the competition at the first hurdle. The Russian upset predictions to reach the final by putting out reigning Olympic Champion " [:a {:href "/athletes/22051"} "Eric Srecki"] " and two other Olympic medallists " [:a {:href "/athletes/21890"} "Jean-Michel Henry"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/22482"} "Iván Kovács"] " on his way. Kovács was a little unlucky in that he slipped and injured an ankle during their bout. The other half of the draw was also prone to upsets and the man who survived to face Beketov was another outsider in the shape of Cuba’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/21548"} "Iván Trevejo"] "."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The final was desperately close with the scores tied on no less than nine occasions. With the scores at 14-14 a lunge from Beketov pushed through the Cuban’s defences and saw him crowned Olympic champion. In an all-Hungarian bronze medal match " [:a {:href "/athletes/22468"} "Géza Imre"] " defeated a still limping " [:a {:href "/athletes/22482"} "Iván Kovács"] "."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Seed"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "18"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/23274"} "Aleksandr Beketov"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/RUS"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: